WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Ask normally
Type a request in Agent and press Enter. The conversation, activity and Owner notebook remain separate.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
What you can do
Save an explanation during work, add your own words, and choose whether to learn, review, reference or delegate.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Open an explanation
Send L-000001 to discuss one recorded insight. It does not replace the original work.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Keep your own memo
Press Enter with an empty Agent input. Write in the yellow Owner memo field and press Enter to save locally.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Review a candidate
Switch back to Agent when ready. Arrow keys and Enter select a candidate-edit choice; adoption and publication are separate actions.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Search the notebook
Empty Enter moves from Memo to Search. Type Offline; clear the query and press empty Enter to return to Agent. Agent does not suggest past records while you type. Type a record title prefix and press Tab to open choices; choose with arrows and press Tab again to insert. Enter sends your typed request without accepting a suggestion. Memo and search keep automatic plain-text suggestions.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Let AI do the work. You choose what to be part of, and what to make your own.
Work in Agent while keeping private thoughts in Owner. Choose which records to bring into a request.

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Inspect context
Enter /context. The local view reports available request accounting; unavailable values are not invented. Press Esc, the return control, or /close. The conversation and reading position remain available.

9
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Resume the next day
Enter /owner resume. Read the recorded purpose, report and your next step. Historical checks do not recheck today’s files.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Read and copy
F5 expands the active pane. Use PgUp/PgDn or wheel to read. Drag to select; F6 copies. Command+C depends on terminal key reporting; Ctrl+C works when a selection is active.
